# Implementation Plan: Pulse Momentum Scanner

The **Pulse** section is designed as a mission-control HUD for the QuanFin Terminal. It will monitor the expanded Stock Universe (2,132+ stocks) in real-time to detect significant market movements before they trend globally.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Performance Overhead**: Scanning all 2,000+ stocks in real-time via individual API calls is expensive. My plan uses a **Batch Multi-Threading** approach in the backend to minimize latency.
> **Refresh Frequency**: What is the preferred refresh rate? (e.g., Every 30 seconds or 1 minute). 

## Proposed Changes

### Backend (Python/FastAPI)

---

#### [NEW] [pulse_service.py](file:///c:/Users/MOHD%20FAIZAM/OneDrive/Desktop/QuanFin_Terminal/backend/app/services/pulse_service.py)
A service to handle the heavy lifting of scanning 2,132 stocks.
- **In-Memory Cache**: Stores the latest "Pulsing" stocks to avoid redundant calculations.
- **Momentum Logic**: Detects RSI breakouts, Volume shockers, and Day High/Low breaches.
- **Batching**: Uses multi-threaded requests to Yahoo Finance/Kotak for 50-stock chunks.

#### [NEW] [pulse.py](file:///c:/Users/MOHD%20FAIZAM/OneDrive/Desktop/QuanFin_Terminal/backend/app/routers/pulse.py)
Router to expose the Pulse Data:
- `GET /api/v1/pulse/active`: Returns the top 20-50 stocks currently showing abnormal activity.
- `GET /api/v1/pulse/volume`: Specifically filters for Volume Shockers.

#### [MODIFY] [main.py](file:///c:/Users/MOHD%20FAIZAM/OneDrive/Desktop/QuanFin_Terminal/backend/app/main.py)
Include the new `pulse` router in the FastAPI application.

